		<category><![CDATA[SpaceX]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=42305</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/grok_bot_costs.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        SpaceXSI is apparently cutting usage limits for its AI agent Grok Bot, less than two weeks after Musk called it his fastest-growing product. The operating costs were "unsustainably high relative to revenue," Musk wrote on X. OpenAI and Anthropic are also tightening their flat-rate plans as they grapple with the high costs of AI agents.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/spacexsi-apparently-cuts-grok-bot-quotas-weeks-after-musk-called-it-his-fastest-growing-product/">SpaceXSI apparently cuts Grok Bot quotas weeks after Musk called it his fastest-growing product</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
